# tests/chat-tools-mixed, as an ENTRY (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): evaluating
# this directory yields the test's ARG TREE, which dev/run-test then runs.
#
# A WORKER TEST, for the same reason as its sibling tests/chat-tools: the
# subject is llm-step's mixed tool queue, and `caos-cli chat` was the client's turn
# loop, which has its own test. std/llm-test/worker-common.sh does the three
# steps that were plumbing.
#
# dev/worker-test, not std/bash: the conversation REF is the completion signal,
# and refs on the server are the one thing caos gives a worker no verb for.
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/worker-test --worker1:@=worker.sh --bash:@=DEEP-DEPS/bash --llm-step:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-step --stub:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-stub --tool:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-test-tool --common:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-test/worker-common.sh
